# Static migration planning artifacts (never commit).
#
# The WHOLE directory, not a list of filenames. It used to be enumerated file by file
# (static-migration-plan.md, prompt/, changelog.md, firebase-setup.md, questionnaire/),
# which meant every NEW working doc was tracked by default -- and on 2026-09-01
# doc/emailjs-setup.md was committed that way before being caught. CLAUDE.md already
# states "doc/ -- entirely git-ignored; nothing under it is tracked", so this makes the
# rule match the documented intent instead of relying on remembering to add a line.
#
# What lives here and why it is not tracked:
#   - the plan, doc/prompt/*, doc/changelog.md -- plans for executing tasks, not
#     reference material. Anything the repo needs long-term goes in a tracked file.
#   - firebase-setup.md, emailjs-setup.md -- do-once owner console checklists. The
#     schema one describes is already committed in dbmgr/firestore.rules, whose header
#     carries the full collection -> legacy-table mapping.
#   - questionnaire/ -- the authored Q&A source. The build converts it into
#     app/content/questions/en/**.json, which IS committed: one copy of the Q&A in the
#     repo, not two. The JSON is a lossy derivative -- items with no A-D options (STAAR
#     griddables, free-response) are not carried over.
#
# BACK doc/ UP OUTSIDE THE REPO. It is not in version control and questionnaire/ is the
# only place the authored sources and the ~74 non-MCQ items exist.
doc/